WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 size:78% position:39%
-Welcome to the show.
-Thank you very much.

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm so happy to have you.
Been a fan of yours

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:03.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a very long time.
-Thank you.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I want to ask
about "The Crown,"

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.007
because I think there's probably
this unfair perception

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.075 size:88% position:44%
that most Americans have
that all British people

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
are obsessed with
the crown and the monarchy

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not the case.
-No.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:16.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
I sort of barely thought
about them for most of my life

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And, yeah, then I --

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, then I had to actually
be one of them.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.789 size:78% position:39%
So I thought I better
read about it a bit.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:23.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:28.361
I mean, my background was
sort of small-R republican

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:33.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
My mum would actively not watc
the Queen's speech

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:33.900 size:84% position:42% line:92%
on a Christmas morning.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, I had no idea
about them at all.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:39.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, what
could possibly go wrong?

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-I always wonder,

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know,
it's very strange.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.613
This is both a historical drama,
but a lot of the key players

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
are, you know,
they're still alive.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Do you think to yourself,

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.417 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"Are they watching?"

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:53.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, also, do you
want them to watch?

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:56.122 line:92%
-It's a very mixed thing.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.624 line:92%
Part of you wants them to watch,

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also part of you
is terrified.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:02.128 line:92%
I mean, I sort of can't imagin

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.630 line:92%
the Queen and Prince Phili

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of, you know,
Netflix and chilling.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I don't...

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I don't know.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:11.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't think about that
Even if it was on BBC,

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.672 size:81% position:41%
I would think they're
probably not watching.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the fact that it's like,
"What's our log-in?"

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-"Where..."

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I forgot the log--"
-It's a generational thing

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I think you're probably --
you might be in the clear.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:24.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In the clear.
-Both you and Olivia Colman,

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:26.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Helena Bonham Carter,
you all also have

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
this interesting job
ahead of you,

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you're taking over parts
from other actors.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:33.193
Matt Smith, who was wonderfu
in the first two seasons -

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you spend a lot of tim
watching him?

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.996
-I've never heard of him.
-No. I think that's best.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you try to watch
what he did?

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or do you think to yourself,
like, "Oh, that'll only

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
get in the way of
what I choose to do?"

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:46.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, like you, I really love
the first two seasons.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.008
I loved what Matt did.
So, yeah, it was actually

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of an amazing resourc
to go back

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
to those first two seasons
and watch,

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:56.516
and then sort of combine tha
with, you know, the real person.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:59.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like 80/20.
-Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:01:59.819 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I think 80/20's good.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what I got
from your performance.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.256 size:78% position:39%
-Okay, thanks, buddy.
-I was like, "That's

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
about 80/20 right there."
-Okay.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:08.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A lot of corgis.
-Yes.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:11.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, there's
a lot of on-set corgis.

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, there are
two on-set corgis.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just only two?
-Yeah.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's a boy corgi
and a girl corgi.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-The girl corgi

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:18.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
is quite mischievous.
-Uh-huh.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:22.375
-Yeah, she very rarely sort of
stays where she's meant to stay.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And when the girl corgi

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
is there, the boy
gets quite mischievous, too.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, often, you have to, like
remove the girl corgi.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.318 size:81% position:41%
And the boy corgi then
is quite well-behaved.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:35.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was there any part
of playing this role

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:38.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
make you long for a life where
you could live as a royal?

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:42.729
-No. No part of me would want to
be a -- absolutely none, yeah.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:45.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It does seem
pretty just depressing.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, just, I mean, obviously
hugely privileged.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I just --
You go into a lot of rooms

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
people are kind of
tongue-tied I imagine.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:57.177
So just this sort of sheer
weight of quantity of chat..

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...is heavy, I think.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
Small talk.
-Right, yeah.

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.582 line:92%
Everybody is going to leav

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
and talk about
how they met you.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And you're never going to

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
go home and tell anybody
who you met.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.856
-No. I imagine they sort o
look at you, like, sort of this.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I imagine that's sort of,

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
yeah, an odd way
to spend your day.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I also think giant rooms
sound really cool

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
until the minute
you're sitting in one.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.365 size:81% position:41%
And then you're like,
"This is really cold."

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, "Can we bring everythin
in a bit?"

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'd love to just get it in?
Also, I feel like you --

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.138 size:78% position:39%
if you were in, like,
Buckingham Palace,

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.940
you're like, "Oh, my God,
I need way more pictures

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
to put up on the wall
and stuff."

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.876 line:92%
-I mean, I hear anecdotally,

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
they kind of hate
Buckingham Palace.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:32.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's why they sort of

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.280
constantly go out to sort of
Scotland and all the other ones.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I mean, I guess
that's the thing.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've always said, if you hav
a Buckingham Palace,

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.319
make sure you have other places.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
How other palaces?
-You got to have

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
a few other palaces when you
get tired of your palace.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is just --
-That's a good rule.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's one of
the hard, fast rules.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You stayed with one of your --

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
I heard you were getting wor
done on your place.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.364 size:81% position:41%
You were staying with
one of your costars --

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
Helena Bonham Carter.
How was that?

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:54.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you know each other well
You must have.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we've gotten to
know each other on the show.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:59.239 line:92%
Yeah, she's a wonderful woman.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:02.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she very kindly took me in
in my hour of need.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
I sort of had a shortfall
for a few weeks.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:07.981
Yeah, we've been doing a sort of
deep meta kind of "Crown,"

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.850 size:84% position:42%
where I sort of live
with Princess Margaret.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:11.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sort of like
an alternate reality.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We stayed in the accents
and everything.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, great.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:17.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was bizarre.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
But as actors,
you have to, yeah.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, it's very important
to do this sort of work.

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:21.995 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.630
-I mean, I hope you can se
the results in the show.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
I think we all did.

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:28.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Queen texted me.
She loved it.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:29.068 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:32.038
So, you know, I first -- I think
I first saw you in "Rome."

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:34.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow, yeah.
-I loved you in "The Terror.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.809 size:88% position:44%
-And very serious stuff.
and then you turned up

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
in "Catastrophe,"
which is a wonderful show,

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
created by Rob Delaney and
Sharon Horgan.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.449 size:84% position:42%
And another great show,
called "This Way Up."

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:46.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are comedies.
which I hadn't seen you in

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yet, even in the comedies,
it seems like

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
you play it very serious.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.558 size:88% position:44%
I mean, I'm essentially
not a very funny person.

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:54.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So the only way I can be funny

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
is if someone brilliant
like Sharon Horgan

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:59.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
or Aisling Bea
write me funny things to say

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I keep my face
quite still.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I say the line.
And apparently it's funny.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-That's how it works.

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And when they
first came to you,

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:08.808
I mean, I think sometimes
there are dramatic actors

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:10.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
who, when they
get a chance at comedy,

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:10.977 line:92%
they think, "Oh, my God, great

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:12.245 size:81% position:41%
Now I can do all these
funny voices I have."

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.479 size:78% position:39%
Did they come to you
and specifically say,

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Just do exactly what you do
in the serious things?"

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, I mean,
I have my faults,

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I have a very clear sens
of how funny I am.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So I know --

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:25.458
I know that I need their help.
and I'm very grateful to the

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.393 size:75% position:38%
for, yeah, making me
occasionally funny.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, great. It pays off great.
You're wonderful in both.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:30.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thanks so much
for being here.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really great to meet you.
-Thank you.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much.
Tobias Menzies, everybody.

